=== FILE: docs/help/46-read-hex-binary-and-base64.md ===
Read Hex, Binary, and Base64 views
Experimental. The reviewed tooltip registry and module index describe byte-oriented representations. Packaged behavior is UNVERIFIED.
Choose Hex, Binary, or Base64 in the representation selector. These views render bytes from the project-owned artifact copies after checking their recorded SHA-256 identities.
They do not encode the decompiled text.
The documented scopes are:
Scope	Meaning
Whole file	File bytes from the beginning of the artifact
Selected function entry	File bytes beginning at a mapped function entry


Function-entry scope does not establish the function’s complete extent. Bytes displayed after its actual end can belong to another function or data.
An entry must map through the PE section table to file-backed bytes. Virtual-only, ambiguous, or out-of-image addresses remain unavailable; a range must not be guessed.
Pages contain 4,096 bytes. Both sides use the same logical page position within their chosen scopes. Different file layouts can place corresponding instructions at different offsets.
Go to offset accepts a hexadecimal file offset and switches to whole-file scope. A file offset is different from an RVA or virtual address.
Check scope, side, offset, and artifact identity when copying observations. Matching page numbers do not establish matching function bodies.
If artifact verification fails, resolve the integrity issue before relying on displayed bytes. Do not bypass it by editing recorded hashes.
Sources: src/patchtrace/tooltips.py, viewer.*; docs/modules.md, artifact bytes and raw view entries.
=== FILE: docs/help/47-preview-and-export-reports.md ===
Preview and export reports
Choose Export or press Ctrl+E to produce a report from saved project data.
1. Select Markdown, HTML, or JSON.
2. Choose the destination file.
3. Decide whether to include function code.
4. Decide whether to include analyst notes.
5. Choose selected findings only when that scope is required.
6. Read the exact preview.
7. Select Write report.
Function code is excluded by default. Analyst notes are included by default. Only selected findings requires a finding selection in the main workspace.
The preview reflects the selected format and options. Changing an option can change the output, so review the final preview before writing.
The documented exporter redacts absolute source paths and excludes raw provider responses, API keys, and complete interpretation context payloads. Inspect names, notes, optional code, and remaining project metadata before sharing.
HTML reports are documented as self-contained escaped content without scripts. That export format is separate from raw Ghidriff JSON.
A report is not a full project backup and cannot substitute for the project’s database, inputs, and run files. A PatchTrace JSON report is also not automatically importable as a Ghidriff comparison.
Write report can create or overwrite the destination. Choose a new filename when preserving an earlier report matters. Cancelling the export dialog writes nothing.
Sources: README.md, “Export and share results”; src/patchtrace/tooltips.py, export.*; docs/specs/ui.md.
